From dd74aee87a6bce91aace3448c5558acfeb2fe5aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 02:39:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] fix(api): fail with 503 when the registry is not
 initialised

get_registry() used to open a fresh in-memory SQLite registry when
init_registry() had not run. A wiring mistake (or a request racing the
shutdown) then wrote resources into process memory that vanished on
restart while the API reported success.

get_registry() now raises ComponentNotReadyError like the other
runtime components. The resource routes take the registry through a
require_registry dependency that maps it to a 503 error envelope with
code REGISTRY_UNAVAILABLE (authentication is still checked first), and
the application lifespan clears the global registry on shutdown so a
stopped app no longer hands out a closed connection. The OpenAPI
document gains a shared ServiceUnavailable response for these routes.
